{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/949596-3e-lunar-homebrew","id":949596,"title":"3e Lunar homebrew","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Lunar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-08-12T16:09:06-07:00","id":949596,"title":"3e Lunar homebrew","content":"Over the past few days I've been gathering up Lunar charms I made for my NPCs and writing up some more, and I've got enough that I felt like sharing my work. This isn't necessarily going to end up as a full homebrew project that will allow for a full variety of PC Lunars (it might, and I have written up provisional chargen and advancement rules, but I'm not going to make any overly ambitious promises), but I figure that at the very least it might be useful for STs looking to add some charms to their Lunar NPCs. My general design philosophy for the charms (which are primarily combat-related so far) has been to<br /> - Evoke predatory imagery - overwhelming strength, preying on the weak, being terrifying and untouchable.<br /> - Nothing shapeshifting-related, for two reasons. First, I want to start with writing a Lunar charmset that can stand on its own and feel Lunary even before adding in the shapeshifting, and second because I haven't figured out how I want to work in shapeshifting yet.<br /> - Make sure it's possible for every physical attribute to stand on its own for a combatant. Having an at least average dexterity score and an excellency is always going to be mandatory for a serious fighter, but it should be possible for a Lunar to just take a whole bunch of strength or stamina charms and both be useful and feel distinct, in the same way that a Solar with melee feels different to a Solar with brawl.<br /> <br /> With that out of the way, here are the charms I've written so far. A lot of them lack flavour text, since this is a work-in-progress, but the mechanics should be fairly sound. Any critique is welcome.<br /> <br /> <b>Strength Charms</b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><b>Burrowing Devil Strike</b><br /> <b>Cost: </b>1m;<b> Mins: </b>Strength 2, Essence 1<br /> <b>Type: </b>Supplemental<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>Withering-only<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms: </b>None<br /> No defence can hold for long against the tremendous force of the Lunar\u2019s blows. When the Lunar makes a <b>withering </b>attack, she may use this Charm to raise her attack\u2019s Overwhelming value by 1 or increase it to equal her Strength, whichever would be higher.<br /> <br /> <b>Ferocious Biting Tooth</b><br /> <b>Cost: </b>1m per die;<b> Mins: </b>Strength 2, Essence 1<br /> <b>Type: </b>Supplemental<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>Dual<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms: </b>Burrowing Devil Strike<br /> When the Lunar makes a <b>withering</b> or <b>decisive </b>attack, she may add extra dice of damage at a rate of one mote per die. She may add up to (Strength) post-soak damage dice to a <b>withering </b>attack, or (Essence) dice to a <b>decisive </b>attack.<br /> <br /> <b>Lion-Stalks-Gazelle Methodology</b><br /> <b>Cost: </b>-;<b> Mins: </b>Strength 2, Essence 1<br /> <b>Type: </b>Permanent<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>None<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Permanent<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms: </b>Ferocious Biting Tooth<br /> When the Lunar makes a <b>withering </b>or <b>decisive </b>attack against an enemy who is in Initiative Crash or suffering from a -2 or worse wound penalty, the number of damage dice she may add with Ferocious Biting Tooth increases by half her Strength, rounded up.<br /> <br /> <b>Undeniable Might</b><br /> <b>Cost: </b>- (1m per die);<b> Mins: </b>Strength 3, Essence 1<br /> <b>Type: </b>Permanent<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>Decisive-only<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Permanent<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms: </b>None<br /> When making a <b>decisive </b>attack, the Lunar may substitute her Strength for her Dexterity on her attack roll. If she does, she may reroll up to (her Essence) 1s on her damage roll, at a cost of one mote per die.<br /> <br /> <b>Claws of the Silver Moon</b><br /> <b>Cost: </b>5m;<b> Mins: </b>Strength 1, Essence 1<br /> <b>Type: </b>Simple<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>None<br /> <b>Duration: </b>One scene<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms: </b>None<br /> The Lunar shapes her anima into fierce silver claws. While this Charm is active, her unarmed attack is considered a medium weapon, deals lethal damage and gains the piercing tag. Additionally, her claws can damage immaterial spirits, though she gains no special ability to see the immaterial. If she wields a weapon, she may extend her anima across it to confer to it the ability to strike dematerialised spirits.<br /> <br /> <b>Thundering Bull Charge</b><br /> <b>Cost: </b>2m, 2i;<b> Mins: </b>Strength 2, Essence 1<br /> <b>Type: </b>Supplemental<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>Uniform<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms: </b>None<br /> The charging Lunar crashes into her foe with tremendous force, sending him flying. When she moves into close range of an enemy and attacks him in the same turn, she may activate this Charm. If the supplemented attack hits, its target is knocked backwards one range band and prone.<br /> <br /> <b>Blade-Rending Claw</b><br /> <b>Cost: </b>3m;<b> Mins: </b>Strength 3, Essence 1<br /> <b>Type: </b>Supplemental<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>Decisive-only<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms: </b>Undeniable Might<br /> When the Lunar makes a <b>decisive </b>attack while on 12+ Initiative, she may strike with such force that any weapon used to block her blow shatters. If her foe successfully parries her attack, his weapon is destroyed outright, or disarmed instead if it is an artifact weapon. This counts as a successful <b>decisive </b>attack, and resets her Initiative to base.<br /> <br /> <b>Legion-Scattering Might</b><br /> <b>Cost: </b>3m;<b> Mins: </b>Strength 2, Essence 1<br /> <b>Type: </b>Supplemental<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>Withering-only<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms: </b>None<br /> When the Lunar makes a <b>withering</b> attack against a battle group, she ignores (Strength) points of soak. If her attack provokes a rout check, that check is made at +1 difficulty.<br /> <br /> <b>Prey-Hobbling Bite</b><br /> <b>Cost: </b>3m;<b> Mins: </b>Strength 2, Essence 1<br /> <b>Type: </b>Supplemental<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>Decisive-only<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms: </b>None<br /> A vicious blow from the Lunar cripples her foe or knocks him senseless, making him easy prey. As long as her <b>decisive </b>attack deals at least 3 levels of damage, her foe suffers a -2 penalty to all dice pools for the remainder of the scene, and an additional -2 penalty on all movement-related actions.<br /> <br /> <b>Limb-Maiming Flourish</b><br /> <b>Cost: </b>3m, 1wp;<b> Mins: </b>Strength 3, Essence 2<br /> <b>Type: </b>Reflexive<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>Decisive-only<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms: </b>Prey-Hobbling Bite<br /> After making a successful <b>decisive </b>attack, the Lunar may exchange up to (Strength) levels of final damage she inflicted upon her foe for a crippling injury of equivalent severity.<br /> <br /> <b>Lightning Stroke Attack</b><br /> <b>Cost: </b>3m, 1wp;<b> Mins: </b>Strength 4, Essence 3<br /> <b>Type: </b>Reflexive<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>Decisive-only<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms: </b>Blade-Rending Claw<br /> When attacked, the Lunar may respond with a reflexive <b>decisive </b>clash attack, which must benefit from Undeniable Might.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Dexterity Charms</b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><b>Hunter-Becomes-Hunted Attitude</b><br /> <b>Cost: </b>4m;<b> Mins: </b>Dexterity 3, Essence 1<br /> <b>Type: </b>Reflexive<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>None<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms: </b>None<br /> When the Lunar successfully spots one or more enemies attempting to hide from her, she may make a reflexive (Dexterity + Stealth) roll to enter concealment. Each character she detected in this way suffers a penalty on his (Perception + Awareness) rolls to detect her equal to the threshold successes she scored against him.<br /> <br /> <b>Rabid Beast Attitude</b><br /> <b>Cost: </b>2m;<b> Mins: </b>Dexterity 1, Essence 1<br /> <b>Type: </b>Reflexive<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>Uniform<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms: </b>None<br /> Being outnumbered only strengthens the Lunar\u2019s warrior spirit. She may invoke this Charm to negate any onslaught penalties she suffers against a single attack. If she successfully defends, she gains Initiative equal to the onslaught penalty negated by this Charm.<br /> <br /> <b>Savage Tiger Strike</b><br /> <b>Cost: </b>3m;<b> Mins: </b>Dexterity 3, Essence 1<br /> <b>Type: </b>Reflexive<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>Counterattack, Decisive-only<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms: </b>None<br /> When an enemy successfully hits the Lunar, she may respond with a <b>decisive </b>counterattack that occurs before her foe rolls damage.<br /> <br /> <b>Foot-Trapping Counter</b><br /> <b>Cost: </b>2i per success;<b> Mins: </b>Dexterity 2, Essence 1<br /> <b>Type: </b>Reflexive<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>None<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms: </b>None<br /> The slightest stumble when fleeing from a Lunar can be fatal. When an enemy attempts to disengage from the Lunar, she may activate this Charm to subtract one success for his roll for each 1 in his result.<br /> <br /> <b>Tiger Fades From Sight</b><br /> <b>Cost: </b>1wp;<b> Mins: </b>Dexterity 3, Essence 2<br /> <b>Type: </b>Simple<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>None<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms: </b>Hunter-Becomes-Hunted Attitude<br /> When the Lunar successfully enters stealth using this Charm\u2019s prerequisite, she may deceive her foes by masking her disappearance. She might enter a building, pass behind a tree or simply lose herself in a crowd, tricking any observers into believing she has only briefly left their sight. Anybody trying to follow her will not notice for at least two rounds, or one minute outside of combat, that he has lost track of her. Using this Charm allows the Lunar to launch an ambush attack against anybody she has fooled, despite them being aware of her presence, as long as she meets the other requirements for an ambush.<br /> <br /> <b>Thousand Claw Infliction</b><br /> <b>Cost: </b>5m, 1wp;<b> Mins: </b>Dexterity 3, Essence 2<br /> <b>Type: </b>Simple<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>Decisive-only<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms: </b>None<br /> Striking with terrible speed, the Lunar makes up to (Essence or 3, whichever is greater) <b>decisive </b>attacks, dividing her Initiative as evenly as possible between them. Each successful attack deals bonus damage to its target equal to his current wound penalty.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Stamina Charms</b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><b>Ox-Body Technique</b><br /> <b>Cost: </b>-;<b> Mins: </b>Stamina 1, Essence 1<br /> <b>Type: </b>Permanent<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>Stackable<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Permanent<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms: </b>None<br /> A Lunar may purchase this Charm to permanently gain extra health levels. The number and type of health levels she gains is based on her Stamina.<br /> At Stamina 1 and 2: One -2 and two -4 health levels.<br /> 3 and 4: Two -2 and two -4 health levels.<br /> 5: One -1, two -2, and one -4 health level.<br /> The Lunar may purchase Ox-Body Technique (Stamina) times. If she increases her Stamina after purchasing Ox-Body Technique, her health levels automatically change to reflect the new rating.<br /> <br /> <b>Armadillo-Shell Method</b><br /> <b>Cost: </b>5m;<b> Mins: </b>Stamina 3, Essence 1<br /> <b>Type: </b>Reflexive<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>None<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Until next turn<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms: </b>Impenetrable Beast Armour<br /> The Lunar ignores all penalties to Defence until her next turn.<br /> <br /> <b>Den Mother Attitude</b><br /> <b>Cost: </b>2m or 2m, 2i;<b> Mins: </b>Stamina 1, Essence 1<br /> <b>Type: </b>Reflexive<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>None<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms: </b>None<br /> When an ally within close range is attacked, the Lunar may reflexively take a defend other action to protect him for two motes. She may also activate this Charm for two motes, two Initiative when an ally at short range is attacked to dash into close range and defend him.<br /> <br /> <b>Bruise-Relief Technique</b><br /> <b>Cost: </b>5m, 1wp;<b> Mins: </b>Stamina 2, Essence 1<br /> <b>Type: </b>Simple<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>None<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms: </b>None<br /> Healing comes naturally to the Lunar Exalted. By spending an hour focusing on forcing her body to recover, the Lunar can heal (Essence or 2, whichever is greater) bashing or lethal health levels. She may walk, hold a conversation and perform light activity during this time, but any significant exertion will interrupt the process, forcing her to start over.<br /> <br /> <b>Cornered Mongoose Attitude</b><br /> <b>Cost: </b>2m;<b> Mins: </b>Stamina 2, Essence 1<br /> <b>Type: </b>Supplemental<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>Withering-only<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms: </b>None<br /> While in Initiative Crash, the Lunar may add one non-Charm success to the attack and damage rolls of a <b>withering </b>attack.<br /> <br /> <b>Bloodied Beast Resurgent</b><br /> <b>Cost: </b>1wp;<b> Mins: </b>Stamina 2, Essence 1<br /> <b>Type: </b>Reflexive<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>None<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms: </b>Cornered Mongoose Attitude<br /> When the Lunar makes a <b>withering </b>attack that causes her to recover from crash, she may activate this Charm to immediately gain the benefits of an Initiative Break.<br /> <br /> <b>Impenetrable Hide Demeanour</b><br /> <b>Cost: </b>-;<b> Mins: </b>Stamina 2, Essence 1<br /> <b>Type: </b>Permanent<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>Withering-only<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Permanent<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms: </b>None<br /> Whenever the Lunar is struck by a <b>withering </b>attack that deals (Stamina) or less damage after her soak is applied, she gains one point of Initiative.<br /> <br /> <b>Apex Predator Ascendant</b><br /> <b>Cost: </b>-;<b> Mins: </b>Stamina 3, Essence 2<br /> <b>Type: </b>Reflexive<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>Decisive-only<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms: </b>Bloodied Beast Resurgent<br /> Whenever the Lunar receives an Initiative Shift and uses the extra action it grants her to make a <b>decisive </b>attack, that attack does not reset her to base Initiative if successful.<br /> <br /> <b>Unstoppable God-Beast Might</b><br /> <b>Cost: </b>3m;<b> Mins: </b>Stamina 3, Essence 2<br /> <b>Type: </b>Perilous, Reflexive<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>Decisive-only<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Reflexive<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms: </b>Impenetrable Hide Demeanour<br /> Whenever an attacker deals (Lunar\u2019s Essence or 3, whichever is higher) or less final levels of damage to her with a <b>decisive </b>attack, his Initiative is reset to 0 instead of its usual base value following that attack, immediately sending him into crash. The Lunar gains the usual Initiative Break bonus for crashing him.<br /> <br /> <b>Halting the Scarlet Flow</b><br /> <b>Cost: </b>6m, 1wp, 2a;<b> Mins: </b>Stamina 4, Essence 2<br /> <b>Type: </b>Reflexive<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>Perilous<br /> <b>Duration: </b>One scene<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms: </b>Bruise-Relief Technique<br /> When the Lunar has taken damage to her -2 or -4 health levels, she may draw her anima into herself to close her wounds. At the end of the round in which she activates this Charm, and each subsequent round, she heals two levels of lethal or bashing damage. This Charm cannot heal -0 or -1 health levels, and ends if the Lunar is crashed.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Appearance Charms</b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><b>Radiant Joy Stance (Puppy Eyes Prana)</b><br /> <b>Cost: </b>4m;<b> Mins: </b>Appearance 2, Essence 1<br /> <b>Type: </b>Supplemental<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>None<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms: </b>None<br /> A Lunar with this Charm exudes an infectious exuberance. When she makes an inspire action to evoke feelings of happiness or similar positive emotions, any character who wishes to spend Willpower to reject her influence must cite a Major or Defining Intimacy in a Decision Point to do so.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Perception Charms</b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><b>Inescapable Hunter Attitude</b><br /> <b>Cost: </b>5m;<b> Mins: </b>Perception 2, Essence 1<br /> <b>Type: </b>Simple<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>None<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms: </b>None<br /> As long as a Lunar with this Charm knows a person\u2019s scent, either from having met him in the past or having access to his clothes or other similar belongings, she may track him across any distance and ignores any penalties to do so. This allows her to contest magic that would normally make tracking impossible.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">My homebrew: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1244979-abyssals-a-shadow-falls\" target=\"_blank\">Abyssals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1065949-infernals-to-rule-in-hell-complete-edition\" target=\"_blank\">Infernals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/781489-ex3-dragon-kings-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Dragon Kings,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1058142-lanaya-s-martial-arts-homebrew-compendium\" target=\"_blank\">martial arts.</a></span>","edited":{"userid":3559,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3559-lanaya","user":"Lanaya","date":". 08-13-2016, 06:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3559-lanaya","name":"Lanaya","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3559_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T17:36:34-07:00","id":949654,"title":"","content":"Ferocious Biting Tooth is competing with the Strength Excellency, which should already be able to add dice to Withering damage rolls.<br /> <br /> I instead choose to go for a Charm that allows the Strength Excellency to be used for Decisive damage rolls... as well as Initiative rolls in general, so that it includes any brawny Gambit like grappling or disarming.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T17:48:58-07:00","id":949660,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/949596-3e-lunar-homebrew?p=949654#post949654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ferocious Biting Tooth is competing with the Strength Excellency, which should already be able to add dice to Withering damage rolls.</div> </div> </div> </div>The strength excellency can't be used on damage rolls, and I'm quite happy with that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">My homebrew: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1244979-abyssals-a-shadow-falls\" target=\"_blank\">Abyssals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1065949-infernals-to-rule-in-hell-complete-edition\" target=\"_blank\">Infernals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/781489-ex3-dragon-kings-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Dragon Kings,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1058142-lanaya-s-martial-arts-homebrew-compendium\" target=\"_blank\">martial arts.</a></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3559-lanaya","name":"Lanaya","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3559_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T18:15:09-07:00","id":949675,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanaya</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/949596-3e-lunar-homebrew?p=949660#post949660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The strength excellency can't be used on damage rolls</div> </div> </div> </div>Why not? The book does not forbid this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Lunar Exalted tap into the raw potential of their Attributes<br /> to bolster their heroic feats, and can add up to<br /> (Attribute) dice to any action. However, with a stunt, they<br /> may add a second Attribute to the limit as long as the<br /> action is described in a way that fits the combination. For<br /> example, a Full Moon rolling (Dexterity + Brawl) to smash<br /> a Dragon-Blooded shikari would normally have a dice<br /> limit of (Dexterity), but could increase this to (Dexterity<br /> + Strength) if he described the attack in a way that evoked<br /> his raw brawn and mighty thews. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T18:40:17-07:00","id":949687,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/949596-3e-lunar-homebrew?p=949675#post949675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why not? The book does not forbid this.</div> </div> </div> </div>The damage roll is not an action. The Strength excellency can't add to it any more than the Melee excellency can.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T18:40:24-07:00","id":949688,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/949596-3e-lunar-homebrew?p=949675#post949675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why not? The book does not forbid this.</div> </div> </div> </div>Same reason that you can't stunt your damage rolls. Excellencies enhance rolled actions, and dealing damage isn't an action. I'm not really looking for RAW debates here though, so I'm just going to say that all of these charms are being written under the assumption that you can't excellency a damage roll and that if people want to discuss that interpretation I'd rather they do it in another thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">My homebrew: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1244979-abyssals-a-shadow-falls\" target=\"_blank\">Abyssals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1065949-infernals-to-rule-in-hell-complete-edition\" target=\"_blank\">Infernals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/781489-ex3-dragon-kings-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Dragon Kings,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1058142-lanaya-s-martial-arts-homebrew-compendium\" target=\"_blank\">martial arts.</a></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3559-lanaya","name":"Lanaya","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3559_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T18:42:52-07:00","id":949689,"title":"","content":"Straight adding 1 die of damage to decisives without a conditional is a bit potent for 1m... ferocious biting tooth now becomes a requirement for builds. And does its upgrade add to that? Cause then you have something that's at essence 1 more effective than Fire and Stones strike, and can be used with any combat ability. It should allow you to add that many extra successes to decisive damage if you are going for something similar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1777-kell_tamer","name":"Kell_Tamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1777_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"389"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T19:29:02-07:00","id":949712,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crumplepunch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/949596-3e-lunar-homebrew?p=949687#post949687\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The damage roll is not an action. The Strength excellency can't add to it any more than the Melee excellency can.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Melee Excellency NORMALLY can't apply to dice-pools which don't involve the Melee Ability, which damage rolls do not.<br /> <br /> Damage rolls DO involve the Strength Attribute.<br /> <br /> Also consider the fact that Lunars CAN use the Stamina Excellency to increase their static soak ratings. If they can't use the Strength Excellency to enhance their withering damage, that creates a clear lop-sidedness in their offensive versus defensive ability.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T19:32:19-07:00","id":949715,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kell_Tamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/949596-3e-lunar-homebrew?p=949689#post949689\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Straight adding 1 die of damage to decisives without a conditional is a bit potent for 1m... ferocious biting tooth now becomes a requirement for builds. And does its upgrade add to that? Cause then you have something that's at essence 1 more effective than Fire and Stones strike, and can be used with any combat ability. It should allow you to add that many extra successes to decisive damage if you are going for something similar.</div> </div> </div> </div>That stands out, but isn't necessarily bad design, especially for an entry-level charm. Excellent Strike is similarly &quot;Whuh-oh!&quot; and a no-brainer on just about any attack roll you make, and (I suspect) for similar reasons of narrative conceit: a Solar swordsman is gonna be REALLY FUCKING GOOD at swordfighting, and will probably hit you if they even halfway care about trying; likewise, anything that takes a solid hit from a Strength-focused Lunar is gonna <i>feel </i>it, assuming there's anything left of them to feel.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1024-thesaurasaurus","name":"Thesaurasaurus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T19:32:52-07:00","id":949716,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanaya</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/949596-3e-lunar-homebrew?p=949688#post949688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Same reason that you can't stunt your damage rolls.</div> </div> </div> </div>Please help me out. I'm looking at the rules for stunting <i>and</i> the rules for resolving withering damage, but I don't see any rule about &quot;no stunting your damage rolls&quot;. Not even for decisive damage resolution.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T19:36:48-07:00","id":949719,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/949596-3e-lunar-homebrew?p=949716#post949716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Please help me out. I'm looking at the rules for stunting <i>and</i> the rules for resolving withering damage, but I don't see any rule about &quot;no stunting your damage rolls&quot;. Not even for decisive damage resolution.</div> </div> </div> </div>The very post you quoted included a bit about me not wanting to derail the thread discussing this, which you helpfully chopped from the quote. Start a new thread if you want to have this debate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">My homebrew: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1244979-abyssals-a-shadow-falls\" target=\"_blank\">Abyssals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1065949-infernals-to-rule-in-hell-complete-edition\" target=\"_blank\">Infernals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/781489-ex3-dragon-kings-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Dragon Kings,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1058142-lanaya-s-martial-arts-homebrew-compendium\" target=\"_blank\">martial arts.</a></span>","edited":{"userid":3559,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3559-lanaya","user":"Lanaya","date":". 08-12-2016, 10:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3559-lanaya","name":"Lanaya","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3559_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T20:07:07-07:00","id":949752,"title":"","content":"I'm actually a bit curious re: Puppy Eyes Prana. Does anyone else feel that 4m just to toss out the target's Minor intimacies is a little steep? I may be very easily off base on this, but it does feel a tad pricey for the effect to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/944864-abyssals-in-death-s-dream-kingdom-homebrew-wip-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Abyssals</a><br /> <br /> My attempt at a homebrew for Abyssals, focusing on unique charms.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11602-five_gee","name":"Five_Gee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11602_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T20:21:25-07:00","id":949764,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanaya</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/949596-3e-lunar-homebrew?p=949719#post949719\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The very post you quoted included a bit about me not wanting to derail the thread discussing this, which you helpfully chopped from the quote. Start a new thread if you want to have this debate.</div> </div> </div> </div>Apologies. I did not deliberately ignore that part of your post, but I did you the discourtesy of not reading all of your post. Sorry.<br /> <br /> Still, if your Charms are going to be built on rules and assumptions not found within the corebook itself, then you should present your rules and assumptions. Which you didn't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T20:26:37-07:00","id":949768,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Five_Gee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/949596-3e-lunar-homebrew?p=949752#post949752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm actually a bit curious re: Puppy Eyes Prana. Does anyone else feel that 4m just to toss out the target's Minor intimacies is a little steep? I may be very easily off base on this, but it does feel a tad pricey for the effect to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not just minor intimacies. Usually you don't need a decision point at all to stop an inspire, you can just decide you don't feel like it and pop a willpower. And since an inspired emotion counts as a major intimacy for persuading purposes, I figured 4m to be able to pretty reliably land them seemed worthwhile. Could well be wrong on that, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">My homebrew: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1244979-abyssals-a-shadow-falls\" target=\"_blank\">Abyssals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1065949-infernals-to-rule-in-hell-complete-edition\" target=\"_blank\">Infernals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/781489-ex3-dragon-kings-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Dragon Kings,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1058142-lanaya-s-martial-arts-homebrew-compendium\" target=\"_blank\">martial arts.</a></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3559-lanaya","name":"Lanaya","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3559_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T20:37:32-07:00","id":949777,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanaya</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/949596-3e-lunar-homebrew?p=949768#post949768\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's not just minor intimacies. Usually you don't need a decision point at all to stop an inspire, you can just decide you don't feel like it and pop a willpower. And since an inspired emotion counts as a major intimacy for persuading purposes, I figured 4m to be able to pretty reliably land them seemed worthwhile. Could well be wrong on that, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, yeah. I did not think about the actual mechanics of an inspire, just saw the decision point and my brain switched into auto pilot.<br /> <br /> That seems appropriate then, ignore me. I was never here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/944864-abyssals-in-death-s-dream-kingdom-homebrew-wip-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Abyssals</a><br /> <br /> My attempt at a homebrew for Abyssals, focusing on unique charms.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11602-five_gee","name":"Five_Gee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11602_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T21:11:55-07:00","id":949799,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kell_Tamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/949596-3e-lunar-homebrew?p=949689#post949689\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Straight adding 1 die of damage to decisives without a conditional is a bit potent for 1m... ferocious biting tooth now becomes a requirement for builds. And does its upgrade add to that? Cause then you have something that's at essence 1 more effective than Fire and Stones strike, and can be used with any combat ability. It should allow you to add that many extra successes to decisive damage if you are going for something similar.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, forgot to reply to this. As <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1024-thesaurasaurus\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1024\" data-vbnamecard=\"1024\">Thesaurasaurus</a> says, Ferocious Biting Tooth being really good is intended. And it is largely better than Fire and Stones Strike, but I think it's overall worse than Solar Brawl's damage boosters, which are my main point of comparison here. My general idea is that Strength charms will be comparable to Brawl and Dexterity charms will be comparable to Melee. The main thing I'm concerned with is that it might be too easy to combine the two in order to get almost-Brawl levels of damage plus almost-Melee levels of everything else, which would be too good, but that's a bridge I'll cross once I've fleshed out the charm trees a bit more. Simply preventing Lunars from combining Strength and Dexterity charms on one action would do the trick, but it's not something I want to do, so hopefully I can figure out a more elegant solution.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">My homebrew: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1244979-abyssals-a-shadow-falls\" target=\"_blank\">Abyssals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1065949-infernals-to-rule-in-hell-complete-edition\" target=\"_blank\">Infernals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/781489-ex3-dragon-kings-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Dragon Kings,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1058142-lanaya-s-martial-arts-homebrew-compendium\" target=\"_blank\">martial arts.</a></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3559-lanaya","name":"Lanaya","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3559_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T21:36:14-07:00","id":949811,"title":"","content":"Apologies again.<br /> <br /> Lanya was right. By the explicit definition, soak is not a static value and thus cannot be enhanced with an Attribute Excellency, so it further makes sense that the Strength Excellency cannot enhance damage rolls.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T06:50:40-07:00","id":950006,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanaya</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/949596-3e-lunar-homebrew?p=949799#post949799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sorry, forgot to reply to this. As <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1024-thesaurasaurus\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1024\" data-vbnamecard=\"1024\">Thesaurasaurus</a> says, Ferocious Biting Tooth being really good is intended. And it is largely better than Fire and Stones Strike, but I think it's overall worse than Solar Brawl's damage boosters, which are my main point of comparison here. My general idea is that Strength charms will be comparable to Brawl and Dexterity charms will be comparable to Melee. The main thing I'm concerned with is that it might be too easy to combine the two in order to get almost-Brawl levels of damage plus almost-Melee levels of everything else, which would be too good, but that's a bridge I'll cross once I've fleshed out the charm trees a bit more. Simply preventing Lunars from combining Strength and Dexterity charms on one action would do the trick, but it's not something I want to do, so hopefully I can figure out a more elegant solution.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem i see with that is something broadly applicable shouldn't be better than something narrowly focused at the narrow focus. Being able to apply to every attack and extra 5 decisive damage with each reset to base regardless of the attack type being used is not only better. It's objectively better in every way. Since at essence one a solar can add 3. Even dividing it by two round up and then having an essence upgrade would help. Comparing it to solar's brawl adders is a different can of worms since solar brawl adders are also largely conditional on the enemy having onslaught, and being able to add extra successes. There is no &quot;just spend motes and do extra damage with no condition on the decisive&quot; charms at essence 1 for decisives.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1777-kell_tamer","name":"Kell_Tamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1777_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"389"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T15:20:27-07:00","id":950247,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kell_Tamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/949596-3e-lunar-homebrew?p=950006#post950006\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem i see with that is something broadly applicable shouldn't be better than something narrowly focused at the narrow focus. Being able to apply to every attack and extra 5 decisive damage with each reset to base regardless of the attack type being used is not only better. It's objectively better in every way. Since at essence one a solar can add 3. Even dividing it by two round up and then having an essence upgrade would help.</div> </div> </div> </div>It can only add one damage to a decisive at E1. The upgrade charm can situationally raise it to a cap of +4 damage, which is a fair bit more impressive, but if I were making a character and had the choice between those two charms or Ferocious Jab + Heaven Thunder Hammer/Vicious Lunge + Crashing Wave Throw, I'd pretty much always want to be taking the Solar charms. It is a delicate balance though, and I may have gone too far with FBT. It's something I'll need to playtest once I've done enough charms to make proper characters.<br /> <br /> In other news, I wrote some grappling charms (and lifted one from the Barbarian Warlord QC).<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><b>Throat-Baring Hold</b><br /> <b>Cost: </b>3m;<b> Mins: </b>Strength 2, Essence 1<br /> <b>Type: </b>Supplemental<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>Decisive-only<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Until the grapple ends<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms: </b>None<br /> Twisting her foe into a vulnerable position, the Lunar exposes the weaknesses in his defences. This Charm enhances a grapple attempt. If the Lunar wins control of the grapple, her target suffers an additional -1 to Defence and a penalty to soak equal to (Lunar\u2019s Essence or 3, whichever is greater) for the duration of the grapple.<br /> <br /> <b>Flesh-Tearing Entanglement</b><br /> <b>Cost: </b>1m;<b> Mins: </b>Strength 3, Essence 2<br /> <b>Type: </b>Reflexive<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>None<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms: </b>Throat-Baring Hold<br /> The Lunar\u2019s foe is torn apart by her iron grip as he tries to escape it. Whenever the Lunar loses a round of control over a grapple as a result of being attacked or taking damage, she may spend one mote to deal one die of lethal damage to the grappled foe.<br /> <br /> <b>Crushing Bear Grip</b><br /> <b>Cost: </b>5m;<b> Mins: </b>Strength 3, Essence 2<br /> <b>Type: </b>Simple<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>None<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms: </b>Throat-Baring Hold<br /> Essence surging through her form, the Lunar holds her foe in an inescapable clinch. When the Lunar makes a control roll, she may convert (Essence or 3, whichever is greater) dice into automatic successes. At Essence 3+, she may spend a point of Willpower when using this Charm in order to grapple foes with the Legendary Size Merit.<br /> <br /> <b>Spine-Breaking Technique</b><br /> <b>Cost: </b>3m, 1wp;<b> Mins: </b>Strength 3, Essence 2<br /> <b>Type: </b>Simple<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>Decisive-only<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms: </b>Crushing Bear Grip<br /> While in a grapple, the Lunar may use this Charm to make a <b>decisive </b>savaging attack without resetting to base Initiative. This Charm may only be used once per scene.<br /> <br /> <b>Jaws of the River Dragon</b><br /> <b>Cost: </b>9m, 1wp;<b> Mins: </b>Strength 5, Essence 4<br /> <b>Type: </b>Simple<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>Decisive-only<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms: </b>Spine-Breaking Technique<br /> As her foe is held helpless in her grasp, the Lunar rips his body asunder and tosses him away. If the Lunar has five or more rounds of control in a grapple, she may expend all her remaining rounds of control to make a <b>decisive </b>savaging attack with double 7s on the damage roll.<br /> <br /> <b>Indomitable Tyrant Grasp</b><br /> <b>Cost: </b>7m;<b> Mins: </b>Strength 5, Essence 5<br /> <b>Type: </b>Supplemental<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>Decisive-only<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms: </b>Jaws of the River Dragon<br /> The Lunar channels the power of Creation\u2019s most feared predators. This Charm enhances a grapple gambit, allowing the Lunar to make her control roll unopposed unless her foe possesses the Legendary Size Merit or uses magic such as Dragon Coil Technique. Even then, her foe must reroll (Lunar\u2019s Strength) successful dice on his control roll. Using this Charm, the Lunar may grapple even the most titanic of foes, though she can only make savaging attacks against such enormous creatures.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">My homebrew: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1244979-abyssals-a-shadow-falls\" target=\"_blank\">Abyssals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1065949-infernals-to-rule-in-hell-complete-edition\" target=\"_blank\">Infernals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/781489-ex3-dragon-kings-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Dragon Kings,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1058142-lanaya-s-martial-arts-homebrew-compendium\" target=\"_blank\">martial arts.</a></span>","edited":{"userid":3559,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3559-lanaya","user":"Lanaya","date":". 08-13-2016, 08:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3559-lanaya","name":"Lanaya","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3559_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T17:04:17-07:00","id":950318,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanaya</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/949596-3e-lunar-homebrew?p=950247#post950247\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It can only add one damage to a decisive at E1. The upgrade charm can situationally raise it to a cap of +4 damage, which is a fair bit more impressive, but if I were making a character and had the choice between those two charms or Ferocious Jab + Heaven Thunder Hammer/Vicious Lunge + Crashing Wave Throw, I'd pretty much always want to be taking the Solar charms. It is a delicate balance though, and I may have gone too far with FBT. It's something I'll need to playtest once I've done enough charms to make proper characters.<br /> <br /> In other news, I wrote some grappling charms (and lifted one from the Barbarian Warlord QC).<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><b>Throat-Baring Hold</b><br /> <b>Cost: </b>3m;<b> Mins: </b>Strength 2, Essence 1<br /> <b>Type: </b>Supplemental<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>Decisive-only<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Until the grapple ends<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms: </b>None<br /> Twisting her foe into a vulnerable position, the Lunar exposes the weaknesses in his defences. This Charm enhances a grapple attempt. If the Lunar wins control of the grapple, her target suffers an additional -1 to Defence and a penalty to soak equal to (Lunar\u2019s Essence or 3, whichever is greater) for the duration of the grapple.<br /> <br /> <b>Flesh-Tearing Entanglement</b><br /> <b>Cost: </b>1m;<b> Mins: </b>Strength 3, Essence 2<br /> <b>Type: </b>Reflexive<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>None<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms: </b>Throat-Baring Hold<br /> The Lunar\u2019s foe is torn apart by her iron grip as he tries to escape it. Whenever the Lunar loses a round of control over a grapple as a result of being attacked or taking damage, she may spend one mote to deal one die of lethal damage to the grappled foe.<br /> <br /> <b>Crushing Bear Grip</b><br /> <b>Cost: </b>5m;<b> Mins: </b>Strength 3, Essence 2<br /> <b>Type: </b>Simple<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>None<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms: </b>Throat-Baring Hold<br /> Essence surging through her form, the Lunar holds her foe in an inescapable clinch. When the Lunar makes a control roll, she may convert (Essence or 3, whichever is greater) dice into automatic successes. At Essence 3+, she may spend a point of Willpower when using this Charm in order to grapple foes with the Legendary Size Merit.<br /> <br /> <b>Spine-Breaking Technique</b><br /> <b>Cost: </b>3m, 1wp;<b> Mins: </b>Strength 3, Essence 2<br /> <b>Type: </b>Simple<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>Decisive-only<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms: </b>Crushing Bear Grip<br /> While in a grapple, the Lunar may use this Charm to make a <b>decisive </b>savaging attack without resetting to base Initiative. This Charm may only be used once per scene.<br /> <br /> <b>Jaws of the River Dragon</b><br /> <b>Cost: </b>9m, 1wp;<b> Mins: </b>Strength 5, Essence 4<br /> <b>Type: </b>Simple<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>Decisive-only<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms: </b>Spine-Breaking Technique<br /> As her foe is held helpless in her grasp, the Lunar rips his body asunder and tosses him away. If the Lunar has five or more rounds of control in a grapple, she may expend all her remaining rounds of control to make a <b>decisive </b>savaging attack with double 7s on the damage roll.<br /> <br /> <b>Indomitable Tyrant Grasp</b><br /> <b>Cost: </b>7m;<b> Mins: </b>Strength 5, Essence 5<br /> <b>Type: </b>Supplemental<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>Decisive-only<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms: </b>Jaws of the River Dragon<br /> The Lunar channels the power of Creation\u2019s most feared predators. This Charm enhances a grapple gambit, allowing the Lunar to her control roll unopposed unless her foe possesses the Legendary Size Merit or uses magic such as Dragon Coil Technique. Even then, her foe must reroll (Lunar\u2019s Strength) successful dice on his control roll. Using this Charm, the Lunar may grapple even the most titanic of foes, though she can only make savaging attacks against such enormous creatures.</div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>Oh not trying to be troublesome. I actually missed the essence limit first pass. Especially since I like lunars, I want to see good homebrew and most the other stuff at a pass seems a ok. I do agree having FBT work on withering helpfully mitigates trying to rule excellencies to handle things. Glad to see the idea of charms working without shape-shifting being necessary.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1777-kell_tamer","name":"Kell_Tamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1777_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"389"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T17:39:28-07:00","id":950330,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure about the strict balance of these, but I see some work I like! In particular the charm which allows you to replace Dexterity with Strength in decisive attack rolls, and Indomitable Tyrant Grasp, of what's written so far.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 08-13-2016, 09:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-14T18:35:24-07:00","id":950835,"title":"","content":"I just realised that I forgot to include the most important grappling charm of them all.<br /> <br /> <b>Bear-Rending Force</b><br /> <b>Cost: </b>5m;<b> Mins: </b>Strength 5, Essence 3<br /> <b>Type: </b>Simple<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>Decisive-only<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms: </b>Spine-Breaking Technique<br /> While grappling an enemy, the Lunar may attempt to tear him asunder. She makes a <b>decisive </b>gambit with a difficulty equal to his remaining health levels and (Essence) bonus dice on the Initiative roll, which deals exactly enough damage to kill him if successful. This horrific execution also counts as an automatically successful inspire action to cause fear in any other enemies who witness it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">My homebrew: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1244979-abyssals-a-shadow-falls\" target=\"_blank\">Abyssals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1065949-infernals-to-rule-in-hell-complete-edition\" target=\"_blank\">Infernals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/781489-ex3-dragon-kings-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Dragon Kings,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1058142-lanaya-s-martial-arts-homebrew-compendium\" target=\"_blank\">martial arts.</a></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3559-lanaya","name":"Lanaya","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3559_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-14T20:31:14-07:00","id":950886,"title":"","content":"Trauma Bear would not approve.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T19:00:29-07:00","id":951433,"title":"","content":"Moving away from bulging muscles and heroics for a moment, here are some manipulation charms.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><b>Two-Tongued Serpent Offering</b><br /> <b>Cost: </b>6m, 1wp;<b> Mins: </b>Manipulation 5, Essence 3<br /> <b>Type: </b>Simple<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>Psyche<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms: </b>???<br /> The Lunar makes a (Manipulation + Presence or Performance) instill attempt to make a single character believe an object in her possession is a priceless treasure. If her roll overcomes the victim\u2019s Resolve, he is utterly enraptured by it, developing a Major Derangement of obsession towards the object, or a Defining Derangement if his permanent Willpower is equal to or less than the Lunar\u2019s Essence. The victim can throw off this compulsion by spending a point of Willpower, but only if he is shown that his fixation with the object is threatening an Intimacy of equal or greater intensity to the Derangement inflicted, or if it has been in his possession for at least an hour. Once a character has been exposed to this Charm, whether he resists or not, he cannot be affected again for the remainder of the story.<br /> <br /> <b>Rapacious Envy Delusion</b><br /> <b>Cost: </b>- (+5m);<b> Mins: </b>Manipulation 5, Essence 3<br /> <b>Type: </b>Permanent<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>None<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Permanent<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms: </b>Two-Tongued Serpent Offering<br /> This Charm enhances its prerequisite, allowing it to be used against multiple targets. Additionally, for an extra five motes the Lunar may infuse the chosen object itself with maddening desire. Anybody who sees it is subject to the effects of Two-Tongued Serpent Offering, even if they were not present when the Lunar activated that Charm. This effect has a duration of one scene.<br /> <br /> <b>Unquestionable Authority Practice</b><br /> <b>Cost: </b>4m;<b> Mins: </b>Manipulation 2, Essence 1<br /> <b>Type: </b>Simple<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>None<br /> <b>Duration: </b>One scene<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms: </b>None<br /> The Lunar acts with such certainty that none think to question her. She can persuade other characters to perform actions that do not require an Intimacy without rolling as long as it would not violate one of their Intimacies \u2013 people will instinctively give her trivial items, part to let her through a crowd or give her non-sensitive information. She may also pass unchallenged through most security. Whenever anyone would stop her from an entering an area, she rolls a (Manipulation + Presence) persuade action, which is considered to exploit a Minor Intimacy. Success convinces him that she is authorised to be there and should not be challenged. However, if her authority is challenged by anybody, this Charm immediately ends and cannot be reactivated for the remainder of the scene.<br /> <br /> <b>Simple Favour Attitude</b><br /> <b>Cost: </b>3m, 4i;<b> Mins: </b>Manipulation 4, Essence 2<br /> <b>Type: </b>Simple<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>None<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms: </b>Unquestionable Authority Practice<br /> Flashing a quick smile, the Lunar humbly asks that her foe lend her his blade \u2013 surely a reasonable request? She makes a (Manipulation + Presence) disarm gambit, rolled against her target\u2019s Resolve instead of his Defence. His Intimacies may modify his Resolve as normal. The Initiative cost of the gambit is replaced by the cost of this Charm. If she succeeds, she takes his weapon instead of casting it aside. If she steals an artifact weapon in this way, she may immediately commit motes to attune to it, breaking her foe\u2019s attunement in the process. This Charm can only be used once per scene.<br /> <br /> <b>Wolf-Shepherds-The-Flock Methodology</b><br /> <b>Cost: </b>6m;<b> Mins: </b>Manipulation 4, Essence 2<br /> <b>Type: </b>Simple<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>Mute<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms: </b>Unquestionable Authority Practice<br /> The Lunar issues commands that others instinctively obey. Once per scene she may make a (Manipulation + War) order action to command an enemy battle group, gaining a +2 bonus instead of a -2 penalty if she attempts to command troops of Poor Drill, and likewise taking a -2 penalty to command troops of Elite Drill. She also takes a -3 penalty if she has already acted against the battle group in the current scene. If her order is successful and another character attempts to give that battle group an order before its next action, it will obey whichever character scored more successes</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">My homebrew: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1244979-abyssals-a-shadow-falls\" target=\"_blank\">Abyssals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1065949-infernals-to-rule-in-hell-complete-edition\" target=\"_blank\">Infernals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/781489-ex3-dragon-kings-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Dragon Kings,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1058142-lanaya-s-martial-arts-homebrew-compendium\" target=\"_blank\">martial arts.</a></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3559-lanaya","name":"Lanaya","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3559_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T20:24:55-07:00","id":951463,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanaya</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/949596-3e-lunar-homebrew#post949596\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- Nothing shapeshifting-related, for two reasons. First, I want to start with writing a Lunar charmset that can stand on its own and feel Lunary even before adding in the shapeshifting, and second because I haven't figured out how I want to work in shapeshifting yet.</div> </div> </div> </div>I consider this a glaring oversight and is one of the reasons 2.Xe lunars were glitched. When making such charmsets, you've got to take into account how transforming into a River Dragon would affect the charms. Doing it later means possibly rewriting very large sections of the Lunar charmset.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Read my shit at my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/271207-sandact6-homebrew-topic\" target=\"_blank\">homebrew</a> topic, 2.5e and 3e material!<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263020-alchemicals-2-0-3e-conversion-charm-design-request\" target=\"_blank\">Play Alchemical's in 3e now</a>, you're welcome.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","name":"Sandact6","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1183_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T23:10:50-07:00","id":951515,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sandact6</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/949596-3e-lunar-homebrew?p=951463#post951463\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I consider this a glaring oversight and is one of the reasons 2.Xe lunars were glitched. When making such charmsets, you've got to take into account how transforming into a River Dragon would affect the charms. Doing it later means possibly rewriting very large sections of the Lunar charmset.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I don't mean that I'm not accounting for the 'drink heart's blood, steal shape' kind of Lunar shapeshifting. I meant the weird shapeshifty charms, things like Hybrid Body Rearrangement that let you do freestyle shapeshifting. I'm not sure whether those should exist or not, and if they do whether they should be sprinkled liberally throughout charm trees or perhaps be the big flashy capstone charms, and whether they should be little changes or big, dramatic ones or all those other things. I don't see anything inherently wrong with a Lunar being able to sprout quills, turn an arm into a tentacle or grow snakes, but when you start sticking them all into one charmset you end up seeing Lovecraftian chimera blobs, which is not what I want out of Lunar charms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">My homebrew: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1244979-abyssals-a-shadow-falls\" target=\"_blank\">Abyssals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1065949-infernals-to-rule-in-hell-complete-edition\" target=\"_blank\">Infernals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/781489-ex3-dragon-kings-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Dragon Kings,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1058142-lanaya-s-martial-arts-homebrew-compendium\" target=\"_blank\">martial arts.</a></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3559-lanaya","name":"Lanaya","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3559_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}